## browse

The plugin ships the **browse** binary, built and published by Anomaly (https://github.com/anomalyco/browse), MIT,
Copyright (c) 2025 opencode. It is not contained in this package: the release carries the pinned binary (gzipped) with its own `LICENSE.browse`,
and `manifest/browse.json` records the release, the target, the binary's SHA-256 and its size. The pinned release
is recorded in `manifest/browse.json` in this package, with the upstream tarball's URL, SHA-256 and size.

The browse browser extension is not shipped or bundled. It is installed by the user from the Chrome Web Store, under
its own listing and terms, and it is licensed MIT by the same project.

## Nothing else

No other third-party code is bundled. The release carries the binary and the licence text above, and nothing else.
